# multiplai-kit — BASE CONFIG TEMPLATE
# Copy to .env and fill in your values:  cp .env.example .env
#
# .env holds the full base config: workspace path, default git identity,
# GH token, container settings, and secrets (API keys for skills).
# .env is gitignored. Loaded by claude.sh on every launch.
#
# NOT TO BE CONFUSED WITH env.example (no dot), which is a DIFFERENT template
# for per-profile overrides (env.work, env.personal — git identity only).
# See README.md → "Environment Configuration" for the full picture.

# === Required ===

# Full ABSOLUTE path to your workspace directory (mounted into container at same path).
# IMPORTANT: Use an absolute path, NOT $HOME — $HOME differs between host and container.
WORKSPACE="/Users/youruser/workspace"

# Git identity
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="Your Name"
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="your@email.com"

# === Deep Research Skill (search API keys) ===
# The deep-research pipeline needs at least one search provider. Tavily is
# the primary; Exa is the secondary (semantic search). Both are free and do
# NOT require a credit card.

# Tavily — 1,000 queries/month free. Sign up: https://tavily.com
# TAVILY_API_KEY="tvly-..."

# Exa — 1,000 requests/month free. Sign up: https://exa.ai
# EXA_API_KEY="..."

# Brave Search — 1,000 queries/month free. Sign up: https://brave.com/search/api/
# BRAVE_API_KEY="BSA..."

# Optional overflow providers (one-time free credits):
# Serper.dev — 50K free credits, $1/1K paid (cheapest overflow). Sign up: https://serper.dev
# SERPER_API_KEY="..."
# You.com — $100 free credit (~20K searches). Sign up: https://api.you.com
# YOU_API_KEY="..."

# === GitHub (optional) ===
# Lets Claude use `gh` CLI inside the container (PRs, issues, CI status).
# Option 1: Set directly
# GH_TOKEN="your-gh-token-here"
#
# Option 2: macOS Keychain (auto-detected if env var not set)
#   security add-generic-password -a "$USER" -s "gh-token" -w "$(gh auth token)" -U

# === Messaging (optional — multiplai-messaging plugin) ===
# Slack: a single user token (xoxp-…). See the slack skill's references/setup.md.
# SLACK_TOKEN="xoxp-..."
#
# Gmail: OAuth is a trio (not one bearer string) — mint once on the Mac host with
# the gmail skill's get_token.py, which prints these three lines to paste here.
# GMAIL_CLIENT_ID="...apps.googleusercontent.com"
# GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET="..."
# GMAIL_REFRESH_TOKEN="1//..."

# === Container settings (optional, ignored in --local mode) ===

# Docker image name
# IMAGE_NAME="claude-multiplai:local"

# Container tooling source — setup.sh fetches container/ from this repo at this
# ref. Override to track a fork or a different version (defaults shown).
# CONTAINER_REPO="https://github.com/spikelab/multiplai-container"
# CONTAINER_REF="v0.2"

# SSH key for build bridge to macOS host (e.g., Swift/Xcode builds)
# SSH_BUILD_KEY="$HOME/.ssh/container_build_key"

# Username for SSH build bridge — your macOS username on the host.
# Required by the skills that shell out to the host (transcribe,
# youtube-transcript, screen-demo, swift-build).
# SSH_BUILD_USER="$USER"

# LLM proxy URL (leave commented out for direct Anthropic API)
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL="http://host.docker.internal:4000"

# Claude credentials file for container auth. Use an absolute path; $HOME is OK
# (expanded when this file is sourced), but not ~ (not expanded inside quotes).
# Override per profile in env.<name> for multi-account setups.
# CLAUDE_CREDENTIALS_FILE="$HOME/.claude-container/credentials.json"

# Gemini CLI credentials directory. Absolute path; $HOME is OK (expanded at
# source time), not ~. Override per profile in env.<name> to use different
# Google accounts per profile. gemini-cli writes OAuth credentials here after
# first interactive login.
# GEMINI_CONFIG_DIR="$HOME/.gemini"

# Docker named volume holding the container's Linux venv. Defaults to a
# per-runtime name derived from this kit checkout's path (basename + path
# checksum), so parallel runtimes never share a venv volume. Set explicitly
# only to pin a specific volume — e.g. KIT_VENV_VOLUME=kit-venv to keep the
# pre-rename volume of an existing install.
# KIT_VENV_VOLUME=

# Multiplai hub (multiplai-gui) — only if you run one. Used by the launcher's
# adoption take-back flow (release-then-resume). URL can also live in
# multiplai.conf; the TOKEN belongs here (secrets stay out of committed files).
# MULTIPLAI_HUB_URL="http://127.0.0.1:8787"
# MULTIPLAI_HUB_TOKEN=""
